WEBVTT

00:00:10.784 --> 00:00:12.151
[scoffs]

00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:13.661
The blue devil.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.630
Donut Lord?
It can talk.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.510
You're not...

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.971
You're not here
to abduct me, are you?

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.530
You abducted me.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.590
Okay, that's a fair point.
What are you?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:39.971
Why are you hiding out
in my garage?

00:00:40.091 --> 00:00:41.591
I needed somewhere safe.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.251
And you're the only person
I could think of, Donut Lord.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.430
Why do you keep
calling me Donut Lord?

00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:46.810
'Cause you talk to donuts.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.610
And then eat them
if they get out of line.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:49.950
Again, fair.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.290
Wait, wait, wait.
Where are all the mushrooms?

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.810
Why am I still on Earth?
What is--

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.050
Oh, no!
I lost my rings.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.050
What?

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.225
[low rumbling]

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.741
What's happening?
Is this your mother ship?

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.221
I'm not in the mood
to get probed.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.500
You think you're worried?
I'm not even wearing pants.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.992
What the...
[brakes hissing]

00:01:18.151 --> 00:01:19.871
[yells]
They're coming for me!
Who's coming for you?

00:01:19.931 --> 00:01:21.871
What's that got to do with me?
I don't have time to explain,

00:01:21.991 --> 00:01:22.991
but you have to help me.

00:01:23.091 --> 00:01:25.290
No, I don't. Why?

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.491
Well, my legs,
which normally
would be classified

00:01:27.491 --> 00:01:29.530
as lethal weapons,
feel like spaghetti.

00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:32.810
I need your help. Please.
It's life or death.

00:01:38.877 --> 00:01:40.662
[sighs]

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.770
Fine. Come with me.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.540
Uh, little help?

00:01:54.443 --> 00:01:56.122
[electronic beeping]

00:01:57.941 --> 00:02:00.060
All right, stay here.
And be quiet.

00:02:00.641 --> 00:02:01.781
Good plan. Great plan!

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:02.941
We're already working
so well together.

00:02:03.161 --> 00:02:04.561
Practically finishing
each other's sentences.

00:02:06.881 --> 00:02:07.881
Okay, bye.

00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:12.201
[Tom] Hello there!

00:02:13.181 --> 00:02:14.341
Can I help you?

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.321
Good morning,
my rural chum.

00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:24.641
I'm... from the power company,
investigating the blackout.

00:02:25.121 --> 00:02:26.921
If you don't mind,
I'd like to take a few readings

00:02:26.921 --> 00:02:28.341
inside your house?

00:02:28.521 --> 00:02:30.021
No kidding?
You're from
the power company?

00:02:30.381 --> 00:02:31.881
Mmm.
Oh, you must know
my buddy Spencer.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.821
We play softball together.
Ah! Spence.

00:02:35.161 --> 00:02:36.221
He's a good man.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.941
Yeah. Come on in!
Great.

00:02:40.361 --> 00:02:41.661
Take all the readings you need.

00:02:41.941 --> 00:02:42.941
Except, uh...

00:02:43.059 --> 00:02:46.502
Doesn't the power company
usually take their readings
from outside the house?

00:02:46.621 --> 00:02:48.641
That way they can check them
even if you're not home.

00:02:49.641 --> 00:02:51.741
Also, my buddy Spencer
works for the gas company,

00:02:52.161 --> 00:02:53.661
and he's more of
an Ultimate Frisbee guy.

00:02:53.781 --> 00:02:56.401
So you want to tell me
why you think I'm dumb enough

00:02:56.401 --> 00:02:58.021
to just let you
walk inside my house?

00:03:00.994 --> 00:03:02.088
[beeping]

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.741
I'm sorry, Mister...
Wachowski.

00:03:09.241 --> 00:03:10.261
But everyone calls me Tom.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.520
Except my dentist,
he calls me Tim.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.441
But it's gone on
for so long now

00:03:14.441 --> 00:03:15.941
that it would just be weird
if I corrected him.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.401
Well, Tom, whose-dentist-
calls-him-Tim.

00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:21.061
You may have noticed
that this entire town

00:03:21.061 --> 00:03:22.901
has been experiencing
a power outage.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:24.820
Yep, no lights.
Picked up on that.

00:03:25.181 --> 00:03:28.081
Twenty minutes ago,
I tracked an energy pulse
with a similar signature

00:03:28.081 --> 00:03:29.521
to the one that caused
that disruption.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.190
Listen, uh, Mister...

00:03:47.051 --> 00:03:48.051
Doctor.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.070
Dr. Robotnik.
But my dentist calls me Rob.

00:03:51.181 --> 00:03:52.839
Hmm.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.030
Look, uh, Dr. Robotskeez.

00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:58.531
Um, I'm sure
what you're here for
is very serious,

00:03:58.710 --> 00:03:59.930
but it's got nothing
to do with me.

00:04:00.011 --> 00:04:01.011
You can ask anyone in town.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.130
Everyone knows me.
I bet they do.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.810
I'm sure you're hella popular

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.850
with the Jebs and Merles
and Billy Bobs,

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.991
in this glorified
gas-station rest stop.

00:04:09.471 --> 00:04:11.770
Betcha go way back
to the days of tippin' cows

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.110
and playin' in a jug band!

00:04:13.215 --> 00:04:16.084
[spitting]

00:04:16.191 --> 00:04:19.071
And maybe someday
you'll achieve your goal

00:04:19.071 --> 00:04:21.931
of getting a Costco card
or adopting a Labradoodle.

00:04:22.091 --> 00:04:24.451
But the reality is,
I surpassed

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.711
everything you're
ever going to do...

00:04:29.271 --> 00:04:30.711
before I was a toddler.

00:04:31.191 --> 00:04:34.531
I was spitting out formulas
while you were
still spitting up formula.

00:04:35.191 --> 00:04:36.491
I was breastfed,
actually.

00:04:37.071 --> 00:04:39.750
Nice.
Rub that in my orphan face.

00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:43.051
Mr. Wachowski,
are you familiar with

00:04:43.311 --> 00:04:46.131
US Code 904,
Title 10, Article 104?

00:04:46.549 --> 00:04:48.012
Yeah, who isn't--
"Anyone...

00:04:48.091 --> 00:04:52.131
who attempts to aid an enemy
of the United States
shall suffer death."

00:04:53.841 --> 00:04:55.680
And if I'm the one
that catches you,

00:04:56.561 --> 00:04:57.781
it'll be even worse.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.940
Worse than death?

00:05:01.069 --> 00:05:03.722
[drones whirring]

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.510
[Sonic] Okay, I'm a ball,
a normal ball.

00:05:05.631 --> 00:05:06.631
I'm blending in like a ball.
[drone beeping]

00:05:06.691 --> 00:05:08.050
Shh. Stop talking.
No, youstop talking.

00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:09.911
Be quiet, Sonic.
Yoube quiet, Sonic.

00:05:10.471 --> 00:05:12.731
Oh, I hope they aren't
scanning me with X-rays.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.770
I had kind of
an embarrassing lunch.

00:05:22.741 --> 00:05:24.741
Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.

00:05:25.821 --> 00:05:27.500
Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.

00:05:28.621 --> 00:05:29.621
I'm freaking out!

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:34.870
Why don't you have
your staircase carpeted?

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.992
[loud clatter]
Compared to what I--

00:05:39.445 --> 00:05:40.871
Old pipes.
Yeah.

00:05:40.971 --> 00:05:42.250
Probably just
the house settling.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.510
Nothing to see here!

00:05:44.951 --> 00:05:45.951
Hey!

00:05:51.241 --> 00:05:52.320
Here's the thing.

00:05:54.441 --> 00:05:55.540
I'm never wrong.

00:05:55.683 --> 00:05:59.237
Well, first time
for everything, I guess.

00:05:59.381 --> 00:06:00.520
Would you like some cake?

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.441
I hear raccoons have
the cleanest mouths

00:06:02.441 --> 00:06:04.080
of any animal that
routinely eats garbage.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.746
[chuckles]

00:06:09.177 --> 00:06:10.710
[floor creaks]

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:17.101
Look at that.

00:06:18.361 --> 00:06:19.521
I was right.

00:06:20.581 --> 00:06:21.981
Note the lack of surprise.

00:06:22.941 --> 00:06:23.941
Shall we try this again?

00:06:24.053 --> 00:06:27.941
[whistling
"Flight of the Valkyries"]

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.901
I'm going to give you
five seconds
to tell me where it is.

00:06:38.989 --> 00:06:40.055
Five...

00:06:40.055 --> 00:06:41.055
I don't know what
you're talking about.

00:06:41.121 --> 00:06:42.520
Four.
Hey, tough guy.
I'm a cop,

00:06:42.621 --> 00:06:43.641
and you're
threatening an officer.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.260
How can you threaten somebody
who never existed?

00:06:45.412 --> 00:06:47.308
Three...

00:06:47.461 --> 00:06:48.941
Come on!
Rack your brain.

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.581
You might be able to come up
with some lame excuse

00:06:51.581 --> 00:06:54.741
to go on living
in two...

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:56.381
one.

00:06:56.921 --> 00:06:58.520
Wait! Don't hurt him!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.520
[shrieks]

00:06:59.562 --> 00:07:00.639
[grunts]

00:07:00.739 --> 00:07:02.455
[rapid beeping]

00:07:03.834 --> 00:07:05.112
[Sonic yelps]

00:07:12.141 --> 00:07:13.441
This feels excessive.

00:07:17.141 --> 00:07:18.260
Stay behind me.

